codex
Stage 4’s independent hash/bijection audit is clean: both domain rules map one-to-one to the two universal conjuncts, the target is their exact conjunction, and every mounted launcher hash matches. The apparent `∧ True` is the exact translation of the source’s `#Ceil(@V)` for an already-sorted `Val`; the material cast-definedness equivalence remains, so it is redundant but does not weaken or replace an obligation.

I’m now creating the mandated fresh proof project. I’ll rebuild from scratch, run the mechanical candidate gate and exact axiom print, then exercise every target parameter with ground counterexamples and deliberately bad replacements.
